module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.FpqcQuasicoherentAffine

/-!
# Towards the affine half of Tag 03DT

`Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_fpqcTopology_over_quasiCoherentPresheaf_of_affine_base` reduces Tag 03DT to
one statement, `haff`: for a ring map `φ : R ⟶ T` with `Spec φ` flat and surjective and for a
quasi-coherent module `F` on `Spec R`, the presheaf of Tag 03DS is a sheaf for the sieve of
`CategoryTheory.Over (Spec R)` generated by `Spec T ⟶ Spec R`.  This file supplies three of the
four ingredients that statement needs.

The first is the **semilinearity of the presheaf of Tag 03DS**: its restriction maps are
semilinear over the restriction maps of the presheaf of global functions.  This is what makes the
pullback-sections presheaf a presheaf of modules in the first place, and it is what lets a general
section be reduced to the canonical generators `1 ⊗ m` of `T ⊗_R Γ(F, ⊤)`.  Supplied here is
`Stacks.Sites.topUnitMap_smul`, the semilinearity of the map on global sections attached to a
comparison of modules; the presheaf-level statement that follows from it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackSectionsMap_smul`, which is proved with the module structure of
Tag 03DU.

The second is the **sieve reduction**: the sieve of `Over Y` attached to the sieve of `Y` generated
by a single morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` is the sieve generated by the single morphism
`Over.mk f ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 Y)`, so the sheaf condition for it is the sheaf condition for a
one-element presieve, which `CategoryTheory.Presieve.isSheafFor_singleton` turns into an
equalizer statement over an arbitrary test object.  This lemma is purely categorical and holds in
any category.

The third is the **value of the comparison on the canonical generators**: under
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionsColimit.sectionsPullbackIso`, the composite of the canonical map
on sections with a further pullback along `Spec α` carries `m` to `1 ⊗ m` again.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.topUnitMap_smul`: the map on global sections attached to a morphism of schemes and
  a comparison of modules is semilinear over the map of global functions.
* `Stacks.Sites.overEquiv_symm_generate_singleton` and
  `Stacks.Sites.isSheafFor_overEquiv_symm_generate_singleton_iff`: the sieve reduction.
* `Stacks.Sites.sectionsPullbackIso_pullbackSectionsMap_specSectionsMap`: the comparison takes the
  canonical generator to the canonical generator.

## Implementation notes

`AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackSectionsMap_smul` is stated for an arbitrary morphism `g : X ⟶ Y` of
`CategoryTheory.Over S`, which is strictly more general than Tag 03DU's clause: that clause is
that lemma instantiated at `toOver.map f` for a functor `toOver : C ⥤ Over S` into the schemes over
`S`, and it carries a quasi-coherence hypothesis on `F` which nothing in the proof uses.  The
module structures are the native ones on `Γ((pullback Y.hom).obj F, ⊤)` over `Γ(Y.left, ⊤)`, which
are the ones Tag 03DU transports along the objectwise identifications of
`AlgebraicGeometry.PullbackSectionsPresheaf`; for `AlgebraicGeometry.quasiCoherentPresheaf` those
identifications are `CategoryTheory.Iso.refl`.

**A sharper form of the cost rule recorded in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Topologies/FpqcQuasicoherentAffine.lean`.**  That
file records that a statement about `AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackSectionsMap` at
`Stacks.Sites.specOverMap` is free in the projection spelling and a kernel timeout in the
`Spec.map` spelling.  The same split occurs one level down, inside the *module structure*:

| statement | cost |
|---|---|
| scalar at `Γ((specOver ψ).left, ⊤)`, map `(specOverMap ψ α χ h).left.appTop` | **2.6 s** |
| scalar at `Γ(Spec T, ⊤)`, otherwise identical | **kernel timeout, > 45 s** |
| element at `ToType (moduleSpecΓFunctor.obj ((pullback (specOver ψ).hom).obj F))` | **> 45 s** |
| element at `ToType Γ((pullback (specOver ψ).hom).obj F, ⊤)` | **2.9 s** |

So the rule for this area is: bind scalars and elements at the *projection* spelling of the
`CategoryTheory.Over` object, and never at `Spec T` or at `moduleSpecΓFunctor.obj`.  The
`moduleSpecΓFunctor` module structure must be entered through
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionsColimit.moduleSpecΓ_smul` inside a proof, where the type of the
intermediate `have` is inferred rather than written out.

## What remains for the affine half of Tag 03DT

Two steps remain.

* The **square at a general section**: the lemma
  `Stacks.Sites.sectionsPullbackIso_pullbackSectionsMap_specSectionsMap` below
  is the case of the canonical generator.  The general case follows from it by
  `TensorProduct.induction_on`, using `AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackSectionsMap_smul` for the scaling
  step; the base-change map on `T ⊗_R Γ(F, ⊤)` should be carried as an opaque function with its
  additivity, its semilinearity and its value on `1 ⊗ m` as hypotheses, because writing it out as
  `ModuleCat.extendScalars` data reintroduces the `RingHom.toAlgebra`-versus-canonical-`Algebra`
  collision on `T ⊗_R T`.
* The **assembly**: with that square, the sheaf condition for the one-element presieve supplied by
  `Stacks.Sites.isSheafFor_overEquiv_symm_generate_singleton_iff` and
  `CategoryTheory.Presieve.isSheafFor_singleton`, tested at `Spec (T ⊗_R T)` with the two
  inclusions, becomes the exactness of the Amitsur complex in degrees at most one, which is proved
  as `Stacks.Descent.exact_mk_rTensor_includeLeftSubRight` together with Mathlib's
  `Module.FaithfullyFlat.tensorProduct_mk_injective`.

